# EKF-active parameter set: one of the EKF-active runs of the P00 probe (both runs use this set since the fork ruling).
#
# The pinned set (compat_base.parm, copied unchanged from the ArduPilot Webots_Python
# example at af852591) sets AHRS_EKF_TYPE 10, which selects the simulator's own state
# as the estimator. This file adds only what is needed to make EKF3 the estimator, so
# the estimator-health item has a configuration in which it means something. Parameter
# files layer in order, so every value this file does not name still comes from the
# pinned set.
AHRS_EKF_TYPE 3
EK3_ENABLE 1
EK2_ENABLE 0

# The three values above are the known-good 15/16 baseline (git 3fb6564, flown as
# accept-mission-10/12: one run per invocation held every waypoint to 2-4 cm while
# the other suffered a mid-hold EKF attitude divergence). Iteration 14's
# compass-less GPS-yaw set (EK3_MAG_CAL 5 + EK3_SRC1_YAW 3, which refused to arm)
# is withdrawn; what follows is the one change-set on top of that baseline.

# Feed the simulator's own pose to EKF3 as ExternalNav. The bridge republishes the
# flight-state packet's position and attitude (the same Webots devices, converted
# with the bridge's enu_to_ned) as MAVLink VISION_POSITION_ESTIMATE, so the
# estimator flies on the simulator-interface truth instead of inferring attitude
# from a synthesized compass and simulated GPS - the synthesis whose mid-hold
# divergence produced the 15/16 runs' single failure (accept-mission-12 run-a:
# "GPS Glitch or Compass error", PreArm "GPS and AHRS differ by 30.0m", crash
# detector at AngErr=170). P01-L later replaces this truth feed with real
# visual-inertial navigation.
#
# Sources, pinned firmware values (libraries/AP_NavEKF/AP_NavEKF_Source.cpp at
# af85259 - @Values lines: "0:None, 3:GPS, 4:Beacon, 6:ExternalNav" for POSXY,
# "... 6:ExternalNav ..." for VELXY, "0:None, 1:Baro, 2:RangeFinder, 3:GPS,
# 4:Beacon, 6:ExternalNav" for POSZ, "0:None, 1:Compass, 2:GPS, 3:GPS with
# Compass Fallback, 6:ExternalNav, 8:GSF" for YAW):
EK3_SRC1_POSXY 6
EK3_SRC1_VELXY 6
EK3_SRC1_POSZ 6
EK3_SRC1_YAW 6
# ExternalNav yaw aligns and fuses from the pose quaternion while stationary
# (AP_NavEKF3_MagFusion.cpp:481-486: alignYawAngle then fuseEulerYaw(EXTNAV)), so
# no compass is needed at any point - unlike GPS yaw, which needs motion, and
# which is why iteration 14's stationary start refused to arm.
#
# The vision messages reach EKF3 only through AP_VisualOdom, which is disabled at
# its default _TYPE 0: handle_common_vision_position_estimate_data returns unless
# AP::visualodom() exists, and AP_VisualOdom::handle_pose_estimate exits while
# !enabled() (AP_VisualOdom.cpp:203-206); only VISO_TYPE 1 (VisualOdom_Type::MAV)
# creates the AP_VisualOdom_MAV backend that calls writeExtNavData
# (AP_VisualOdom.cpp:135-141, AP_VisualOdom_MAV.cpp:47).
VISO_TYPE 1
# Webots R2025a exposes no compass device; the synthesized magnetometer leaves the
# fusion entirely. No MAG_CAL line: its default 0 needs no external-yaw
# grandfathering, and the pinned rule that rejected iteration 14
# (AP_NavEKF3.cpp:1176-1184, MAG_CAL 5/6 inconsistent with a non-GPS yaw source)
# is not exercised.
COMPASS_USE 0
